it's official war zone is a free-to-play  upgraded version of blackout with new  modes and features here's everything you  need to know about the standalone Call  of Duty game first of all war zone has  two game modes battle royale and plunder  battle royale is mostly the blackout you  remember but it now supports a hundred  and fifty players you can drop onto the  map and solos duo's and trios scavenge  for weapons and other gear and fight to  be the last soldier standing but let's  say you get downed the first time you  get eliminated you'll be sent to a new  location called the Gulag if you manage  to beat another eliminated player in a  1v1 shootout you'll be able to redeploy  you'll find cash across the battle  royale map - this can be spent at buy  stations which are marked on the map  with a shopping cart  Activision says you'll be able to  purchase things like kill streaks  redeploy tokens to revive your teammates  and kits for reviving yourself - then  there's plunder where your goal is to  actually make the most money you'll get  cash from looting stealing from other  players and completing objectives called  contracts there are several kinds of  contracts to fulfill recon contracts for  example tasks you withholding a control  point on the map similar to domination  mode both of these modes take place on  the same map a big city called for dansk  according to Activision it has 300  different points of interest and they  range from dense city blocks to more  open rural areas you can get around the  map on several vehicles - players can  ride on an ATV offering little  protection but high speed the tactical  Rover is also fast and mostly  unprotected but four players can ride  together  the SUV can also seat four players but  it does trade some speed for more  protection the slowest of these grounded  vehicles is the cargo truck which holds  your full squad and equipment and offers  high defense  lastly you can take to the skies in a  four seater helicopter Activision hasn't  announced for persons squads to  accompany some of these vehicles but  it's possible we'll see them added in  the future so when can you play warzone  the game launches for ps4 Xbox one and  PC on March 10th and to reiterate it is  free to play activision expects it to go  live around noon Pacific time  standalone game weighs in between 83 and  110 gigabytes if you don't own modern  warfare already if you do own it you'll  be able to jump in a little earlier you  can download the warzone update around a  much smaller 20 gigs and jump in at 8:00  a.m. Pacific it's also worth noting that  your battle pass items operators weapons  and customization items will all carry  over for modern warfare into warzone  progress owned in warzone also counts  toward your overall multiplayer rankings  and there's no level cap in warzone  what's more if you download it by itself  and pick up modern warfare down the road  your progress and rewards will also  transfer backwards so that's everything  you need to know about Call of Duty war  zone expect to see more coverage and  gameplay on GameSpot and we'll see you  in the city or at least in the gulag
 

